  "question": "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 \\end{bmatrix}$, find $|2A|$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "First compute $|A|$.<br />$|A| = (1)(4) - (3)(2)$.<br />$= 4 - 6 = -2$.<br />For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, $|kA| = k^2 |A|$.<br />Substitute $k=2$.<br />$|2A| = 2^2 \\times (-2)$.<br />$= 4 \\times (-2)$.<br />$= -8$.",
